  "quikchat-backend/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the steps to build a multi-stage Docker image for the QuikChat backend application, resulting in a small, production-ready image.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a Dockerfile and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Multi-stage Build: Uses a `golang:1.21-alpine` image for building and an `alpine:latest` image for the final runtime, reducing image size.\n  - Dependency Caching: Downloads Go modules in a separate step to leverage Docker layer caching.\n  - Static Compilation: `CGO_ENABLED=0` ensures a statically linked binary.\n  - Port Exposure: Exposes port 8080 for the application.\n  - Command: Sets the default command to run the compiled `quikchat` binary.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/README.md": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/README.md`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an overview, architectural details, and instructions for setting up and running the QuikChat backend locally.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a documentation file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Documentation: Describes the project's language, architecture, database, cache, API type, and local setup steps using Docker Compose.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/api/swagger.yaml": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/api/swagger.yaml`\n- High-Level Purpose: A placeholder file for the OpenAPI (Swagger) specification of the QuikChat API.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a specification file and currently contains minimal placeholder information for the API title, version, and description. It does not define any actual API paths yet.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/cmd/api/main.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/cmd/api/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the QuikChat backend API server. It handles application bootstrapping, including configuration loading, database connection, dependency injection, server startup, and graceful shutdown.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `main()`: Public function that serves as the application's entry point. It initializes the logger, loads configuration, connects to PostgreSQL, sets up repositories, services (use cases), HTTP handlers, and the Chi router. It then starts the HTTP server in a goroutine and implements graceful shutdown on OS signals.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Application Bootstrapping: Orchestrates the setup of all major components.\n  - Dependency Injection: Components like repositories, services, and handlers are created and passed their dependencies.\n  - Graceful Shutdown: Uses `os.Signal` and `context.WithTimeout` to ensure the server shuts down cleanly.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/docker-compose.yml": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/docker-compose.yml`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines and configures a multi-container Docker application for the QuikChat backend, including the Go application, a PostgreSQL database, and a Redis instance.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Services**:\n    - `backend`: The Go application service, built from the `Dockerfile`, exposed on port 8080, depends on `db` and `redis`, and mounts the local directory.\n    - `db`: A PostgreSQL 15-alpine database service, exposed on port 5432, with persistent data volume and health checks.\n    - `redis`: A Redis 7-alpine service, exposed on port 6379, with persistent data volume and health checks.\n  - **Volumes**:\n    - `postgres_data`: A named volume for PostgreSQL data persistence.\n    - `redis_data`: A named volume for Redis data persistence.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Docker Compose: Orchestrates multiple Docker containers.\n  - Service Health Checks: Ensures dependent services are ready before starting.\n  - Volume Mounting: Persists data for the database and Redis.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/go.mod": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the module path and manages external Go dependencies for the QuikChat backend project.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Module Declaration**:\n    - `module quikchat`: Declares the module path for the project.\n  - **Dependencies**:\n    - `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.0.12`: HTTP router.\n    - `github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5 v5.2.1`: JWT library.\n    - `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.5.5`: PostgreSQL driver.\n    - `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1`: Loads environment variables from `.env` files.\n    - `golang.org/x/crypto v0.22.0`: Cryptographic utilities, including bcrypt.\n  - **Indirect Dependencies**: Lists transitive dependencies required by the direct ones.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/user_handler.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/handler/user_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for user-related operations such as registration, login, and fetching current user details, interacting with the `UserUseCase`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `UserHandler`: Holds a `usecase.UserUseCase` instance to perform business logic.\n      - Fields: `userService` (usecase.UserUseCase).\n    - `RegisterRequest`: Represents the request body for user registration.\n      - Fields: `Username` (string), `Password` (string).\n    - `LoginRequest`: Represents the request body for user login.\n      - Fields: `Username` (string), `Password` (string).\n    - `AuthResponse`: Represents the response body for successful authentication.\n      - Fields: `AccessToken` (string), `RefreshToken` (string).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewUserHandler(userService usecase.UserUseCase) *UserHandler`: Public constructor function for `UserHandler`.\n  - **Methods**:\n    - `Register(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `UserHandler`. Handles new user registration requests, decodes the request body, calls the `userService.Register` method, and responds with the created user or an error.\n    - `Login(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `UserHandler`. Handles user login requests, decodes the request body, calls the `userService.Login` method, and responds with access and refresh tokens or an error.\n    - `GetCurrentUser(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `UserHandler`. Retrieves the `user_id` from the request context (set by authentication middleware) and returns it.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/router/router.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/handler/http/router/router.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Configures and returns the main HTTP router for the application, defining API routes and applying middleware.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `New(userHandler *handler.UserHandler, jwtSecret string) http.Handler`: Public function that initializes and returns a `chi.Router` instance. It applies global middleware (like `RequestLogger`) and defines public authentication routes (`/api/v1/auth/register`, `/api/v1/auth/login`) and protected routes (`/api/v1/me`) with JWT authentication middleware.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Chi Router: Uses the `go-chi/chi` library for routing.\n  - Middleware Application: Demonstrates how to apply middleware globally and to specific route groups.\n  - Route Grouping: Organizes routes into public and protected groups.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/user_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/user_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `UserRepository` interface for PostgreSQL, providing concrete database operations for user data.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `UserRepository`: Holds a database connection pool.\n      - Fields: `db` (*pgxpool.Pool).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewUserRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) *UserRepository`: Public constructor function for `UserRepository`.\n  - **Methods**:\n    - `Save(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method on `UserRepository`. Inserts a new user record into the `users` table and updates the user's ID.\n    - `FindByUsername(ctx context.Context, username string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method on `UserRepository`. Queries the `users` table to find a user by their username. Returns `nil, nil` if not found.\n    - `FindByID(ctx context.Context, id int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method on `UserRepository`. Queries the `users` table to find a user by their ID. Returns `nil, nil` if not found.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/domain/user.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/domain/user.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the `User` domain entity structure, representing a user in the QuikChat application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `User`: Represents a user entity with various attributes.\n      - Fields: `ID` (int64), `Username` (string), `PasswordHash` (string, marked to be ignored in JSON), `DisplayName` (string), `ProfileImageURL` (*string), `CreatedAt` (time.Time), `UpdatedAt` (time.Time), `LastSeenAt` (*time.Time).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Domain Model: Represents a core business entity.\n  - JSON Tagging: Uses `json:\"...\"` tags for JSON serialization/deserialization, including `json:\"-\"` to hide sensitive fields.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/repository/user_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/repository/user_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for user data persistence operations, abstracting the underlying storage mechanism.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Interfaces**:\n    - `UserRepository`: An interface defining methods for interacting with user data storage.\n      - `Save(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method to save a new user.\n      - `FindByUsername(ctx context.Context, username string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a user by username.\n      - `FindByID(ctx context.Context, id int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a user by ID.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/service/user_service.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/service/user_service.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the business logic for user-related operations, acting as a use case handler that interacts with the `UserRepository` and utility functions.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `userService`: Implements the `UserUseCase` interface, holding dependencies for user repository, JWT secret, and token expiry durations.\n      - Fields: `repo` (repository.UserRepository), `jwtSecret` (string), `accessTokenExpiry` (time.Duration), `refreshTokenExpiry` (time.Duration).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewUserService(repo repository.UserRepository, jwtSecret string, accessExp, refreshExp time.Duration) *userService`: Public constructor function for `userService`.\n  - **Methods**:\n    - `Register(ctx context.Context, username, password string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method on `userService`. Handles user registration by checking for existing users, hashing the password, creating a new user domain object, and saving it via the repository.\n    - `Login(ctx context.Context, username, password string) (accessToken, refreshToken string, err error)`: Public method on `userService`. Handles user login by finding the user, checking the password hash, and generating access and refresh JWTs.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/usecase/user_usecase.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/usecase/user_usecase.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for user-related business logic (use cases) within the application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Interfaces**:\n    - `UserUseCase`: An interface defining methods for user registration and login.\n      - `Register(ctx context.Context, username, password string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to register a new user.\n      - `Login(ctx context.Context, username, password string) (accessToken, refreshToken string, err error)`: Public method to authenticate a user and issue tokens.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000001_create_users_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000001_create_users_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the initial `users` table and an index for the QuikChat backend database.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `users`: Table to store user information.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `username` (VARCHAR(50), UNIQUE, NOT NULL), `password_hash` (VARCHAR(255), NOT NULL), `display_name` (VARCHAR(50), NOT NULL), `profile_image_url` (VARCHAR(255)), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `last_seen_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ).\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_users_username`: An index on the `username` column of the `users` table for efficient lookups.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/config/config.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/config/config.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Handles loading and parsing application configuration from environment variables, with support for `.env` files and default values.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `Config`: Holds all application configuration parameters.\n      - Fields: `Port` (int), `DatabaseURL` (string), `RedisAddress` (string), `JWTSecretKey` (string), `AccessTokenExpiry` (time.Duration), `RefreshTokenExpiry` (time.Duration).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Load() (*Config, error)`: Public function that loads configuration from environment variables (and `.env` file if present), parses them, and returns a `Config` struct.\n    - `getEnv(key, fallback string) string`: Internal helper function to retrieve an environment variable or return a fallback value.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/logger/logger.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/logger/logger.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a utility function to create a structured logger using Go's `slog` package.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `New(w io.Writer) *slog.Logger`: Public function that creates and returns a new `slog.Logger` instance. It configures the logger to use a JSON handler and sets the default logging level to `LevelDebug`.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/auth.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/auth.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an HTTP middleware function for authenticating requests using JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) from the Authorization header.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Auth(jwtSecret string) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. It extracts the JWT from the \"Authorization\" header, validates it using the provided secret, and if valid, adds the `user_id` from the token claims to the request context before calling the next handler.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Middleware: Implements the standard `http.Handler` interface for chaining request processing.\n  - JWT Authentication: Validates tokens and extracts user information.\n  - Context Propagation: Stores the authenticated user's ID in the request context for downstream handlers.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/logger.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/logger.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an HTTP middleware function to log details of incoming requests.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `RequestLogger(next http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. It logs the HTTP method, path, duration, and remote address for each request before passing it to the next handler.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Middleware: Implements the standard `http.Handler` interface for chaining request processing.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/util/hash.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/util/hash.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for securely hashing passwords and comparing plain text passwords against hashes using bcrypt.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `HashPassword(password string) (string, error)`: Public function that takes a plain text password and returns its bcrypt hash.\n    - `CheckPasswordHash(password, hash string) bool`: Public function that compares a plain text password with a bcrypt hash, returning `true` if they match, `false` otherwise.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/util/token.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/util/token.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for generating and validating JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) with custom claims.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `JWTClaims`: Custom claims structure for JWTs, embedding `jwt.RegisteredClaims`.\n      - Fields: `UserID` (int64), `jwt.RegisteredClaims`.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `GenerateToken(userID int64, expiry time.Duration, secretKey string) (string, error)`: Public function that creates a new JWT for a given user ID, expiry duration, and secret key.\n    - `ValidateToken(tokenString string, secretKey string) (*JWTClaims, error)`: Public function that parses and validates a JWT string using the provided secret key. Returns the `JWTClaims` if valid, or an error otherwise.\n"
